      <div type="clause" n="15.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 15.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.2" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe rihte lage ⁊ rihtne do<hi rend="italic">m</hi> forsace, beo se scildig wið ðone þe hit age: swa wið cyningc CXX scill', swa wið eorl XL<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.2-4"/> scill', swa wið unræd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3-4"/> XXX scill', swá wið ælc þara, gif hit swa gewurðe, on Engla lage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.dagger"/><pb n="320" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe rihte lage ⁊ rihtne dom forsace, beo se scyldig wið þone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.1-4"/> þe hit áge: swa wið cyningc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.2-3"/> CXX scyll'<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3-3"/>, swa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.4-2"/> wið eorl LX scyll'<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3-3"/>, swa wið hundred XXX scyll'<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3-3"/>, swa wið ælc þæra, gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.5-2"/> hit swa geweorðeþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.6-2"/>, on Engla lage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="320" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe rihte lage ⁊ riht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.1-2"/> dóm forsace, beo se scyldig wið ðone ðe hit age: swa wið cyng<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.2"/> hundtwelftig scill', swa wið eorl syxtig scill', swa wið hundred XX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3"/> scill', swa wið ælc ðára, gyf hit swa geweorðeð, on Engla lage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="320" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe rihte lage ⁊ rihtne dom forsace, beo se scyldig wið þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.1-5"/> þe hit age: swa wið cyningc CXX scyll', ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.2-5"/> swa wyð eorl LX scill', swa wið hundred XXX scill', swa wið ælc ðæra, gif hit swa geweorðeð, on Engla lage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="321" ed="#liebermann"/>Et qui rectę legi uel iusto iudicio refragabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.1-3"/>, reus habeatur erga eum cui pertinebit: <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.2-2"/>erga regem sic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/> CXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.4"/> solidis, sic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/> erga comitem LX solidis, sic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/> erga hundretum XXX solidis, sic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.5"/> erga singulum eorum, si sic accidat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.6"/>, in Anglorum lege.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="321" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui rectum iudicium et iustam legem abnegat, sit forisfactus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.1-6"/> ei cui iustum est: si regi, det<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.2-6"/> illi XL<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.dagger-2"/> solidos, si comiti XX solidos, si hundredo X solidos, si contra omnes hos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.3-5"/>, omnibus reddat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="321" ed="#liebermann"/>Quisquis uero iustam legem et iustum iudicium recusauerit, reus sit erga illum qui presidet, siue erga regem CXX sol., siue erga comitem XL solidorum, siue erga centenarium XXX sol. in lege Anglorum, siue quemque eorum, si sic contigerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="15a.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="182" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ se ðe rihte lage ⁊ riht dóm<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.robnote.fn.2"/> forsace, beo se scyldig wið ðone ðe hit age, swa wið cyng hundtwelftig scill', swa wið eorl syxtig scill', swa wið hundred XXX<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.robnote.fn.3"/> scill', swa wið ælc ðára, gyf hit swa geweorðeð, on Engla lage.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="260" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And se ðe rihte lage and rihtne dom forsace, beo se scyldig wið þone þe hit age: swa wið cyningc CXX scyllinga, swa wið eorl LX scyllinga, swa wið hundred XXX scyllinga, swa wið ælc þæra, gyf hit swa geweorðeþ, on Engla lage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="320" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.1"/> wer richtige Satzung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.2"/> und rechtes Urtheil<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.3"/> zu befolgen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.4"/> weigert, der sei nach<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.5"/> Engländer-Recht schuldig gegenüber dem, welchem es [das Empfangen der Busse für Ungehorsam gegen das Gericht] gehört<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.6"/>: entweder gegenüber dem König 120 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.7"/> oder dem Grafen 60 (40<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.8"/> <hi rend="italic">D Cons</hi>.) Schill. oder der Hundertschaft 30<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.9"/> Schill. oder jedem derselben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_15-2.lnote.de.10"/>, wenn es [das Trotzen gegen alle drei] so vorkommt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever refuses [to obey] just law and right judgment, let him be liable to the one to whom it belongs [to receive the fine for disobeying the court]: either to the king 120 shillings, or to the earl 60 (40, D Cons.) shillings, or to the hundred 30 (20, B) shillings, or to each of them, if it so happens, under English law.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="183" ed="#robertson"/>And he who refuses [to observe] just laws and just judgments shall forfeit, in districts under English law, [a fine] to the party who is entitled thereto—either 120 shillings to the king, or 60 shillings to the earl, or 30 shillings to the hundred<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-2.robnote.n.2"/>, or to all of them, if they are all concerned.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="464" ed="#whitelock"/>And he who refuses to follow just law and just judgment, is to be liable to pay [a fine] in the area under English law to him who has a right to it, either to the king 120 shillings, or to the earl 60 shillings, or to the hundred 30 shillings, or to each of them, if it so happens.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="261" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And in areas under English law, anyone who rejects just laws and judgments is to be liable to the proper authority: either one hundred twenty shillings to the king, sixty shillings to the earl, thirty shillings to the hundred, or to all of them if it is relevant.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="320"><ref target="clause:IIIEm_6-2">III Em 6.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">*Vgl. III Em. 6, 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_24-1">II Cn 24.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_42">Leis Wl 42</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_42-1">Leis Wl 42.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-063">Cn 1018 26–27</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 15:2-3: Cn 1018 26-27</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="195"><label>same fine</label> <ref target="clause:Hu_7">Hu 7–7.1</ref> <quote>we have here the same 30s fine for defiance as we meet later under Cnut (2 d, b)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-063">Cn 1018 26–26.4</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">D's ‘unræd’ should be ‘hundred’. Liebermann compares III Em 6.2.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 321, October 2026 (MS Cons); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 260 / 261, October 2026 (was “xxx: xx”, now “XXX: XX”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">XXX: XX B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nach</hi> 24, 1 possidet <hi rend="italic">zu ändern? Das Folgende bis</hi> 18 <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to be altered to possidet, following 24, 1? What follows, up to 18, is lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15-2.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so; viell.</hi> rihtdom?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic; perhaps rihtdom?</seg></note>
